= Boot Process for BIOS

:toc: left
:icons: font
:sectlinks:
:data-uri:

See also: link:index.html[Main Boot Page], link:efi-boot.html[EFI Boot Process], link:../roadmap.html[Roadmap]

[cols="1,1,3",options="header"]
|===
|Phase |Component |Description

|Stage 1
|Boot sector
|BIOS loads this at `0x7C00`. Which then loads stage2 base on patched variables at VLSP or jump directly if El-Torito.

|Stage 2 (Real Mode)
|Memory detection
|Queries the BIOS for usable memory regions and builds a Multiboot2 Boot Information structure at `0x6000` which is passed to the protected mode stage2 and kernel.

|Stage 2 (Real Mode)
|A20 gate
|Enables the A20 line so memory above 1 MB can be addressed.

|Stage 2 (Real Mode)
|Video setup
|Detects the available outputs (VBE, VGA graphics, VGA text, UART) and selects the preferred one.

|Transition
|GDT setup
|Defines a Global Descriptor Table with flat 4 GB code and data segments.

|Transition
|Protected mode switch
|Flips the CPU from 16-bit real mode to 32-bit protected mode and sets up a stack at `0x9FC00`.

|Stage 2
|Filesystem init
|Initializes the filesystem driver module (corefs) with the BIOS drive list and the partition label/UUID patched in at install time. The driver probes the partition table (MBR/GPT), finds the matching partition and mounts it.

|Stage 3
|Dynamic loading
|Reads `/boot/libTheBootloader-<version>_<config>.so` through the corefs filesystem into a fixed 512 KiB window at `0x100000`, patches the "VLSO" callback structure and resolves the ELF relocations in place.

|Stage 3
|Boot menu
|Parses `/boot/TheBootloader.conf` (profiles, default entry, timeout) and draws the boot menu.

|Future
|Kernel loading
|Load the kernel ELF and hand control over to it. Not yet implemented.
|===

== Memory Map

Stage1, stage2 and the corefs module are in the first megabyte of
conventional memory. Stage3 is loaded exactly at 1MiB, with a fixed 512 KiB window. 

image::bios-boot-memory-map.svg[BIOS/i686 boot memory map]

Key addresses:

* `0x07C00` — stage1 boot sector
* `0x07E00` — stage2 (`core.bin`)
* `0x90000` — corefs module
* `0x9FC00` — stage2 stack top
* `0x100000` — stage3 buffer and kernel start

=== Low memory used by disk.S

`boot/bios/i686/disk.S` runs its real-mode half below 1 MiB. The 16-bit thunk
is copied there on every call, so these addresses are in use during any disk
operation (we use BIOS int 13h):

[cols="1,1,4",options="header"]
|===
|Address |Size |Purpose

|`0x00500`
|88 Bytes
|16-bit real-mode thunk, copied out of the corefs module by `x86_Int13_Thunk` (`thunk_start` to `thunk_end`)

|`0x00600`
|22 Bytes
|INT 13h parameter block, `TP_IN_AX` through `TP_IN_SI`

|`0x07000`
|16 Bytes
|AH=42h Disk Address Packet

|`0x07C00`
|—
|real-mode stack top (`SS=0`, `SP=0x7C00`), grows down
|===

The 32-bit half of `disk.S` stays in the corefs module at `0x90000`. `0x00500` and `0x00600`
alias the VBE buffers that `detect.S` fills.

=== Kernel loading (future)

The kernel is loaded at `0x100000`, the same address as the stage3 buffer, which means stage3 will be overwritten by the kernel. Therefore, stage3 will perform a handoff.

. Stage 3 copies some of the code of itself to lower memory region that is unused.
. It loads the kernel to `0x100000` and jumps to the kernel with multiboot info.

== Current Implementation Status

* Stage 1: Full MBR bootsector with LBA INT 13h support, El Torito no-emulation detection and metadata patching via the "VLSP" signature
* Stage 2: A20 gate, GDT, protected mode switch, video output (VBE/VGA/VGA text/UART), corefs filesystem init, stage3 dynamic loading and configuration parsing — implemented; stops at the boot menu
* Stage 3: Implemented as `libTheBootloader.so` (filesystem access, config parsing, boot menu), loaded into the window at `0x100000`
* Kernel loading and the final handoff: Not yet implemented; the planned trampoline handoff is described above

